# Analects Book 11 (先進) — draft, first half: lemmata 0–37 = passages 11.1–11.20. Token format as the pilot:
#   tokens separated by " | "; a token is  CHARS[PUNCT][=pinyin][/context gloss[//char gloss//char gloss]]
#   a leading "^" breaks the verse line before the token.
# Punctuation is editorial (the edition has none) and always trails the word before it.
# Pinyin defaults to the glossary's first reading; every polyphone states its reading here, and so does
# every character not yet in the glossary.
# Passages follow Zhu Xi's chapter breaks (凡二十五章): 11.1 = units 0–1, 11.2 = 2–3 (Zhu Xi prints the
# list of the four branches in the same chapter as 從我於陳蔡), 11.3–11.6 = 4–7, 11.7 = 8–9, 11.8 = 10,
# 11.9 = 11–13, 11.10 = 14–16, 11.11 = 17, 11.12 = 18–19, 11.13 = 20–22, 11.14 = 23–24, 11.15 = 25–27,
# 11.16 = 28–29, 11.17 = 30–33, 11.18 = 34–35, 11.19 = 36, 11.20 = 37.
# Quotation marks balance within every unit. Where a speech runs on past one of Zhu Xi's comments (11.1
# unit 1, 11.9 unit 13, 11.12 unit 19, 11.18 unit 35) the continuation is left unquoted, Chinese and
# English alike (as Books 8–9).
# Readings decided: 行 xíng in 德行 (unit 3; Zhu Xi 去聲 = xìng, modern practice xíng — note says so);
# 行行 hàng hàng (18; Zhu Xi 胡浪反, agreeing with modern practice); 從 cóng in 從我 (2) and 從者 (11) —
# Zhu Xi marks both 去聲 (zòng, 'to go along as attendant'); modern practice reads cóng, as 3.24; 三 sān
# in 三復 (6; Zhu Xi 去聲, as 5.19); 妻 qì (6); 說 yuè (4); 閒 jiàn (5, 去聲); 好 hào (7); 亡 wú (7); 為 wéi
# (7 'to be', 8/9 'to make', 20 'to work on', 23 奚為); wèi (13 ×2, 28; Zhu Xi 去聲); 喪 sàng (10); 予 yú;
# 夫 fú 'that, those' (13, 16, 22; Zhu Xi 音扶 at 13 and 22; 16 unmarked, read the same); 夫 fū in 大夫;
# 樂 yuè 'music' (0) and lè (18, 音洛); 長 cháng (20, 長府); 中 zhòng (22, 35; 去聲); 與 yǔ 'and' (25),
# yú (26, 平聲), yǔ 'to approve' (37; Zhu Xi 而與之); 參 shēn (31); 辟 pì (32; Zhu Xi 婢亦反); 喭 yàn (33,
# 五旦反); 空 kòng 'in want' (34; Zhu Xi 空匱, no mark; classical dictionaries give kòng for 'poor, in want', many say kōng — note hedges);
# 由 written Yóu in English throughout (as 2.17, 5.6, 6.6; Book 9 printed 'You'); 億 yì; 車 chē; 語 yǔ; 知 zhī; 道 dào; 弟 dì in 弟子, 昆弟.
# Glyphs kept as printed: 徳 (3), 顔 (throughout; so 顔回, 顔路 need keys beside 顏回), 閒 (5), 椁 (8, 9),
# 𦵏 (14, 15; U+26D4F = 葬 zàng).
